winemac.drv: present OpenGL windows through the window surface while child windows cover them.

The OpenGL view of a window is composited above the window surface, which also holds the
pixels of the window's GDI child windows (for instance embedded CEF/Chromium panels), so
those children are invisible over an OpenGL window. winex11.drv solves the same problem
with offscreen rendering (client_surface.offscreen + present(hdc)); winemac.drv ignored
the hdc and never went offscreen.

With this change, while visible child windows overlap the client area of an OpenGL
window:
- macdrv_client_surface_update() marks the client surface offscreen;
- SwapBuffers reads the finished frame from the drawable's own back buffer, saving and
  restoring the read framebuffer, read buffer, pixel pack buffer and pack parameters;
- win32u then calls present(hdc), which copies the frame into the window surface with
  the child windows clipped out, and keeps the GL view hidden.
Without such children nothing changes: the GL view is presented as before, with no copy.
Vulkan and D3DMetal surfaces are not affected.

Tested on Wine 11.0 from the CrossOver 26.2.0 sources, macOS 26, Apple Silicon.
AI-assisted; review before use.

